{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771218351103,"sessionID":"ses_39b28f7acffeLHlrypWKneG5Bj","part":{"id":"prt_c64d733f10010Ej3Bi1XtSd2zv","sessionID":"ses_39b28f7acffeLHlrypWKneG5Bj","messageID":"msg_c64d72015001qLqlW02wJiF95J","type":"tool","callID":"call_0e6c610ac4894e7797a83e76","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md","offset":1130,"limit":500},"output":"<path>/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>1130: - Integrated into Game.tsx to toggle settings panel\n1131: - Follows existing patterns for timeout management and cleanup\n1132: - All 341 tests passing\n1133: \n1134: **Technical Decisions:**\n1135: \n1136: - Uses useRef for tap tracking (avoid re-renders)\n1137: - Implements resetTapState function inside useEffect closure for access to refs\n1138: - Configurable threshold zone for corner detection\n1139: - Supports both touch (touchstart) and mouse (click) events\n1140: - Prevents default on touch events to avoid conflicts with game controls\n1141: - Cleanup removes event listeners and clears timeout\n1142: - Time window: 500ms between taps (standard gesture timing)\n1143: \n1144: **Test Coverage:**\n1145: \n1146: - All existing 341 tests continue to pass\n1147: - Gesture detection verified through manual testing\n1148: - Hook follows React best practices for event handling\n1149: \n1150: **Implementation Summary (Export/Import JSON):**\n1151: \n1152: - Implemented Export JSON button in SettingsPanel footer\n1153: - Implemented Import JSON button with hidden file input\n1154: - Export creates downloadable JSON file (gol-expert-settings.json)\n1155: - Import loads JSON file with validation\n1156: - Comprehensive validation for all expert settings parameters\n1157: - Error message display for invalid imports\n1158: - File format: JSON with pretty-printing (2-space indentation)\n1159: - Blob-based file download with URL.createObjectURL\n1160: - FileReader API for file upload\n1161: - All 349 tests passing\n1162: \n1163: **Technical Decisions:**\n1164: \n1165: - Export uses Blob and URL.createObjectURL for download\n1166: - Pretty-printed JSON with 2-space indentation\n1167: - Import validates against all parameter ranges\n1168: - Custom validation function returns detailed error messages\n1169: - Hidden file input triggered via button click\n1170: - Error state managed in component state\n1171: - Invalid settings prevent import with user feedback\n1172: \n1173: **Validation Coverage:**\n1174: \n1175: - Movement detection: centroidHistoryLength (3-10), movementThreshold (0.1-2.0), minClusterSize (1-5)\n1176: - Scoring: moverPointsPerGeneration (1-100), oscillatorPointsPerGeneration (0-20), scoreMultiplier (0.1-5.0)\n1177: - Level generation: baseTimeSeconds (10-120), timeIncrementPerLevel (0-60), baseFlux (5-50), difficultyScalingMode (TIME_ONLY, RESOURCE_ONLY, MIXED, EXTREME)\n1178: - Grid sizing: mobileCellSize (14-24), desktopCellSize (16-28), minVisibleCells (≥1)\n1179: - Audio: enabled (boolean), volume (0-0.5), waveform (sine, triangle, square, sawtooth)\n1180: \n1181: **Test Coverage:**\n1182: \n1183: - All existing 349 tests continue to pass\n1184: - Export functionality verified through manual testing\n1185: - Import functionality verified with valid and invalid JSON files\n1186: - Error handling tested for malformed JSON\n1187: \n1188: ### 5.2 Presets System (LOW - Convenience)\n1189: \n1190: - [x] Implement preset configurations\n1191:   - Easy: Lower difficulty, generous resources\n1192:   - Normal: Balanced gameplay\n1193:   - Hard: Strict time/flux limits\n1194:   - Chaos: Extreme parameters, unpredictable\n1195: - [x] Implement preset selection UI\n1196:   - Dropdown in Expert Settings\n1197:   - Preview preset values\n1198: - [ ] Add custom preset support\n1199:   - Allow users to save current settings as preset\n1200:   - Name and save custom configurations\n1201:   - NOT YET IMPLEMENTED\n1202: \n1203: **Dependencies**: Expert settings\n1204: \n1205: **Implementation Summary:**\n1206: \n1207: - Implemented Preset type in src/types/index.ts with four preset options: EASY, NORMAL, HARD, CHAOS\n1208: - Implemented src/lib/presets.ts library with applyPreset(), getPresetDescription(), and preset configurations\n1209: - Created four preset configurations with balanced parameter sets:\n1210:   - EASY: Generous Flux (30), longer time limits (90s), lenient scoring (15pt movers, 3pt oscillators), lower movement threshold (0.3)\n1211:   - NORMAL: Balanced Flux (20), standard time limits (60s), standard scoring (10pt movers, 2pt oscillators), standard movement threshold (0.5)\n1212:   - HARD: Limited Flux (15), shorter time limits (40s), strict scoring (8pt movers, 1pt oscillators), higher movement threshold (0.7)\n1213:   - CHAOS: Extreme Flux (10), very short time limits (30s), chaotic scoring (5pt movers, 1pt oscillators), low movement threshold (0.1), larger grid sizing (28px desktop, 22px mobile)\n1214: - Updated SettingsPanel.tsx to include preset selector with description at top of panel\n1215: - Updated SettingsPanel.css with preset section styling\n1216: - Updated createInitialExpertSettings() in src/lib/state.ts to use NORMAL preset by default\n1217: - Added comprehensive test suite with 11 tests covering all presets and edge cases\n1218: - All tests passing (360 total)\n1219: \n1220: **Technical Decisions:**\n1221: \n1222: - Preset type defined as enum-like string union: 'EASY' | 'NORMAL' | 'HARD' | 'CHAOS'\n1223: - applyPreset() performs deep clone using JSON.parse(JSON.stringify()) to prevent mutation issues\n1224: - getPresetDescription() returns human-readable description for each preset explaining the balance and intended difficulty\n1225: - Preset selector placed at top of SettingsPanel for easy access and visibility\n1226: - Preset descriptions use glassmorphism styling with subtle background for readability\n1227: - Default preset is NORMAL for balanced gameplay experience\n1228: - All preset parameters validated against spec-defined ranges\n1229: - Preset application immediately updates all expert settings without requiring panel close/reopen\n1230: - Preset configurations include all expert settings: movement detection, scoring, level generation, grid sizing, and audio parameters\n1231: \n1232: **Test Coverage: 11 tests**\n1233: \n1234: - Preset type definition: 1 test\n1235: - EASY preset configuration: 1 test\n1236: - NORMAL preset configuration: 1 test\n1237: - HARD preset configuration: 1 test\n1238: - CHAOS preset configuration: 1 test\n1239: - applyPreset() deep clone behavior: 1 test\n1240: - applyPreset() applies correct values: 1 test\n1241: - getPresetDescription() returns correct descriptions: 3 tests (EASY, NORMAL, HARD, CHAOS)\n1242: - Invalid preset handling: 1 test\n1243: \n1244: **Integration Notes:**\n1245: \n1246: - Presets integrated into SettingsPanel as dropdown selector at top of panel\n1247: - Preset selector onChange handler calls applyPreset() to update expert settings\n1248: - Preset descriptions displayed below selector to explain each preset's characteristics\n1249: - createInitialExpertSettings() now uses applyPreset('NORMAL') for default configuration\n1250: - Preset system works seamlessly with existing settings persistence (localStorage)\n1251: - Users can manually tweak parameters after selecting a preset for further customization\n1252: - Total test count: 360 tests passing (up from 349)\n1253: \n1254: **Implementation Summary (Tooltips/Documentation & Danger Zone):**\n1255: \n1256: - Added comprehensive help text for all expert settings parameters\n1257: - Each setting now has italicized help text explaining its purpose and valid range\n1258: - Added danger zone section at bottom of settings panel with red warning theme\n1259: - Implemented Chaos Multiplier control (0.5-10.0x) for scoring difficulty scaling\n1260: - Implemented Timer Speed control (0.5-5.0x) for level time countdown speed\n1261: - Updated ExpertSettings type to include optional chaosMultiplier and timerSpeed fields\n1262: - Updated all preset configurations (EASY, NORMAL, HARD, CHAOS) with danger zone defaults\n1263: - Added validation for danger zone parameters in both SettingsPanel.tsx and settings.ts\n1264: - Added CSS styling for danger zone with warning banner and red-themed controls\n1265: - All 360 tests passing\n1266: \n1267: **Technical Decisions:**\n1268: \n1269: - Help text uses italicized styling with reduced opacity for subtle readability\n1270: - Danger zone placed at bottom of settings panel with distinct visual styling\n1271: - Red border and warning banner signal extreme/dangerous settings\n1272: - Danger zone controls use red-themed slider thumbs for visual distinction\n1273: - Defaults: chaosMultiplier=1.0, timerSpeed=1.0 for balanced gameplay\n1274: - Preset danger zone values: EASY (0.5x, 0.8x), NORMAL (1.0x, 1.0x), HARD (1.5x, 1.5x), CHAOS (3.0x, 2.5x)\n1275: - Optional fields in ExpertSettings type (chaosMultiplier?, timerSpeed?) for backward compatibility\n1276: - Validation prevents extreme values: chaosMultiplier (0.5-10.0), timerSpeed (0.5-5.0)\n1277: \n1278: **Test Coverage:**\n1279: \n1280: - All existing 360 tests continue to pass\n1281: - Preset tests updated to include new danger zone fields\n1282: - Settings validation tests include danger zone parameter checks\n1283: - Integration verified through manual testing\n1284: \n1285: **Implementation Notes:**\n1286: \n1287: - Danger zone settings allow experienced players to customize extreme game modes\n1288: - Help text makes expert settings more accessible to new players\n1289: - Visual hierarchy separates normal settings from dangerous ones\n1290: - Changes propagate through existing preset and settings persistence systems\n1291: \n1292: ---\n1293: \n1294: ## Sprint 6: Quality Assurance\n1295: \n1296: _Goal: Stability, accessibility, and performance_\n1297: \n1298: ### 6.1 Error Handling & Resilience (MEDIUM - Stability)\n1299: \n1300: - [x] Implement global error boundary (COMPLETED 2026-02-16)\n1301:   - Catch React component errors\n1302:   - Display user-friendly error message\n1303:   - Log error details\n1304: - [x] Add input validation\n1305:   - Validate all user inputs\n1306:   - Validate configuration parameters\n1307:   - Prevent NaN and infinity\n1308: - [ ] Handle edge cases gracefully\n1309:   - Empty grid states\n1310:   - Zero flux scenarios\n1311:   - Invalid level numbers\n1312:   - Corrupted localStorage\n1313: - [ ] Add retry mechanisms\n1314:   - Retry failed operations with exponential backoff\n1315:   - Graceful degradation when features fail\n1316: - [ ] Handle browser compatibility\n1317:   - Check for required APIs (Web Audio, Canvas)\n1318:   - Fallbacks for unsupported features\n1319:   - Clear error messages\n1320: \n1321: **Dependencies**: All systems\n1322: \n1323: **Implementation Summary (Error Boundary):**\n1324: \n1325: - Implemented ErrorBoundary class component in src/components/ErrorBoundary.tsx with comprehensive error handling\n1326: - Implemented getDerivedStateFromError lifecycle method to catch React errors and set error state\n1327: - Implemented componentDidCatch lifecycle method to log error details to console\n1328: - Implemented user-friendly error UI with \"Something went wrong\" message and reload button\n1329: - Implemented development-only error details section showing error message, component stack, and stack trace\n1330: - Created ErrorBoundary.css with glassmorphism styling matching application theme\n1331: - Added ErrorBoundary.test.tsx with 4 comprehensive tests covering all error scenarios\n1332: - Integrated ErrorBoundary into App.tsx to wrap all application components\n1333: - Error boundary displays reload button that refreshes the page to recover from errors\n1334: \n1335: **Technical Decisions:**\n1336: \n1337: - Used class component (instead of function component) to implement getDerivedStateFromError lifecycle method\n1338: - Error details only shown in development mode (import.meta.env.DEV) for security\n1339: - Reload button uses window.location.reload() to fully refresh the application state\n1340: - Console.error called with both error object and component stack for debugging\n1341: - Glassmorphism design matches other UI components for consistent look and feel\n1342: - Error boundary positioned with z-index: 999999 to overlay all content\n1343: \n1344: **Test Coverage: 4 tests**\n1345: \n1346: - ErrorBoundary renders children when no error occurs\n1347: - ErrorBoundary catches errors and displays error UI\n1348: - ErrorBoundary logs error and component stack to console\n1349: - ErrorBoundary reload button is clickable and displayed\n1350: \n1351: **Integration Notes:**\n1352: \n1353: - ErrorBoundary wraps entire App component to catch all React errors\n1354: - All 364 tests passing (including 4 new ErrorBoundary tests)\n1355: - Error boundary prevents white screen crashes by providing user-friendly error UI\n1356: - Development mode shows detailed error information for debugging\n1357: - Production mode shows simplified error message for better user experience\n1358: \n1359: ### 6.2 Accessibility (LOW - Inclusivity)\n1360: \n1361: - [ ] Implement keyboard navigation\n1362:   - Arrow keys for grid navigation\n1363:   - Enter/Space to place cells\n1364:   - Escape to cancel/close panels\n1365:   - Tab navigation through UI controls\n1366: - [ ] Add screen reader support\n1367:   - ARIA labels for UI elements\n1368:   - Announce game state changes\n1369:   - Alternative text for visual elements\n1370:   - Live regions for score/timer updates\n1371: - [x] Implement reduced motion support\n1372:   - Respect prefers-reduced-motion media query\n1373:   - Disable animations when requested\n1374:   - Simplified visual feedback\n1375: - [ ] Add high contrast mode\n1376:   - Toggle for high contrast colors\n1377:   - Larger text option\n1378:   - Improved readability\n1379: - [ ] Ensure minimum touch targets\n1380:   - 44×44px minimum for mobile\n1381:   - Spacious clickable areas\n1382: - [ ] Focus management\n1383:   - Visible focus indicators\n1384:   - Logical tab order\n1385:   - Focus trap in modals\n1386: \n1387: **Dependencies**: UI components, user interaction\n1388: \n1389: **Implementation Summary (Reduced Motion Support):**\n1390: \n1391: - Added @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) queries to all 10 CSS files\n1392: - Disabled all animations (keyframe animations, transition properties, transform animations) when reduced motion is preferred\n1393: - Covered 76 animation/transition instances across entire codebase\n1394: - Files updated: VictoryScreen.css, IntroOverlay.css, TransitionOverlay.css, SettingsPanel.css, GlassHUD.css, ScoreDisplay.css, LevelStats.css, FluxDisplay.css, index.css, ErrorBoundary.css\n1395: - Prioritized disabling infinite animations (glitch, pulse-glow, pulse) as they cause most vestibular issues\n1396: - Simplified visual feedback for users with motion sensitivity by removing all motion\n1397: - All 364 tests passing with reduced motion support enabled\n1398: \n1399: **Technical Decisions:**\n1400: \n1401: - Used CSS @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) query to detect user's motion preference\n1402: - Set animation: none and transition: none for all animated elements when reduced motion is preferred\n1403: - Set transform: none for hover/active states to prevent scale animations\n1404: - Applied overrides at end of each CSS file to ensure they take precedence\n1405: - Maintains full functionality while removing all motion effects\n1406: - Respects OS-level accessibility settings for users with vestibular disorders or motion sensitivity\n1407: \n1408: ### 6.3 Performance Optimization (LOW - Performance)\n1409: \n1410: - [ ] Implement performance monitoring\n1411:   - FPS counter (development only)\n1412:   - Memory usage tracking\n1413:   - Component render profiling\n1414: - [ ] Add performance optimizations\n1415:   - Memoize expensive calculations\n1416:   - Virtualize large lists (if applicable)\n1417:   - Lazy load non-critical components\n1418:   - Debounce/throttle frequent operations\n1419: - [ ] Profile and optimize\n1420:   - Identify performance bottlenecks\n1421:   - Optimize critical paths\n1422:   - Ensure 60fps with 500+ cells\n1423:   - Test on low-end devices\n1424: - [ ] Implement lazy loading\n1425:   - Load audio on first interaction\n1426:   - Lazy load expert settings panel\n1427:   - Code splitting for production\n1428: \n1429: **Dependencies**: All systems\n1430: \n1431: ### 6.4 Testing (LOW - Quality Assurance)\n1432: \n1433: - [ ] Set up testing framework\n1434:   - Choose testing framework (Vitest recommended)\n1435:   - Configure test environment\n1436:   - Set up coverage reporting\n1437: - [ ] Write unit tests for simulation engine\n1438:   - Rule application (born/survive)\n1439:   - Toroidal boundaries\n1440:   - Age tracking\n1441:   - Edge cases (empty grid, static patterns)\n1442: - [ ] Write unit tests for phase management\n1443:   - Phase transitions\n1444:   - Guard conditions\n1445:   - Timer accuracy\n1446: - [ ] Write unit tests for flux management\n1447:   - Placement and refund logic\n1448:   - Phase-based behavior\n1449: - [ ] Write unit tests for movement detection\n1450:   - Connected component detection\n1451:   - Centroid tracking\n1452:   - Classification accuracy\n1453: - [ ] Write unit tests for scoring system\n1454:   - Score calculation accuracy\n1455:   - Score cap handling\n1456:   - High score persistence\n1457: - [ ] Write unit tests for level progression\n1458:   - Level configuration generation\n1459:   - Difficulty scaling\n1460: - [ ] Write integration tests\n1461:   - End-to-end game flow\n1462:   - Level progression\n1463:   - Score calculation\n1464:   - UI interaction\n1465: - [ ] Add manual testing procedures\n1466:   - Mobile responsiveness\n1467:   - Touch interaction\n1468:   - Audio on different browsers\n1469:   - Performance with high cell counts\n1470:   - Accessibility testing\n1471: \n1472: **Dependencies**: All implemented systems\n1473: \n1474: ### 6.5 Documentation (LOW - Knowledge Transfer)\n1475: \n1476: - [ ] Write README.md\n1477:   - Project overview\n1478:   - Installation instructions\n1479:   - Controls and gameplay guide\n1480:   - Configuration options\n1481:   - Known issues and limitations\n1482: - [ ] Add code comments\n1483:   - Complex algorithms (movement detection, simulation)\n1484:   - State machine logic\n1485:   - Performance-critical sections\n1486: - [ ] Document API interfaces\n1487:   - Component props\n1488:   - Utility functions\n1489:   - Configuration schemas\n1490:   - Type definitions\n1491: - [ ] Create developer guide\n1492:   - Architecture overview\n1493:   - How to add new features\n1494:   - Debugging tips\n1495:   - Common patterns\n1496: - [ ] Document expert settings\n1497:   - Each parameter explanation\n1498:   - Recommended values\n1499:   - Impact on gameplay\n1500: \n1501: **Dependencies**: All implemented systems\n1502: \n1503: ### 6.6 Code Quality & Refinement (COMPLETED - 2026-02-16)\n1504: \n1505: **Goal**: Fix lint errors, improve code quality, and ensure production readiness\n1506: \n1507: - [x] Fixed lint errors and code quality issues\n1508: - [x] Fixed clearTimeout not being recognized as global (changed to window.clearTimeout)\n1509: - [x] Added missing globals to ESLint config (Blob, URL, FileReader, HTMLInputElement)\n1510: - [x] Created separate vitest.config.ts to fix build error\n1511: - [x] Fixed 'any' types in SettingsPanel component (use Record<string, unknown>)\n1512: - [x] Removed unused error variable in catch block\n1513: - [x] Fixed synchronous setState in effects for FluxDisplay, ScoreDisplay, and Game components\n1514: - [x] Refactored levelStats from state to computed value using useMemo\n1515: - [x] Added eslint rule override to allow 'any' types in test files\n1516: - [x] All verification completed (360 tests passing, build successful, TypeScript clean)\n1517: \n1518: **Implementation Summary:**\n1519: \n1520: - Fixed clearTimeout global recognition issue by using window.clearTimeout throughout codebase\n1521: - Added missing browser globals to ESLint configuration: Blob, URL, FileReader, HTMLInputElement\n1522: - Created vitest.config.ts to separate test configuration from main Vite config, resolving build conflicts\n1523: - Replaced 'any' types in SettingsPanel component with Record<string, unknown> for proper type safety\n1524: - Removed unused error variable from catch block to satisfy ESLint no-unused-vars rule\n1525: - Fixed synchronous setState warnings in React effects:\n1526:   - FluxDisplay: wrapped setState in useCallback with proper dependency tracking\n1527:   - ScoreDisplay: wrapped setState in useCallback with proper dependency tracking\n1528:   - Game: refactored levelStats from state to computed value using useMemo\n1529: - Added eslint rule override for test files to allow 'any' types when needed for test doubles\n1530: \n1531: **Technical Decisions:**\n1532: \n1533: - Used window.clearTimeout to ensure global recognition across all environments\n1534: - Created separate vitest.config.ts to isolate test environment configuration from production build\n1535: - Record<string, unknown> provides better type safety than 'any' while maintaining flexibility\n1536: - useMemo for levelStats prevents unnecessary re-computation and state updates\n1537: - useCallback for setState functions ensures stable references across renders\n1538: - ESLint overrides for test files scoped to .test.ts and .spec.ts extensions only\n1539: \n1540: **Verification Results:**\n1541: \n1542: - All 360 tests passing\n1543: - Build successful (npm run build)\n1544: - TypeScript compilation clean (npm run typecheck)\n1545: - ESLint passing (npm run lint)\n1546: - Git tag 0.1.5 created and pushed\n1547: \n1548: ---\n1549: \n1550: ## Parallel Development Tracks\n1551: \n1552: ### Track A (Can start after Project Setup):\n1553: \n1554: - Type definitions → Shared utilities → All other systems\n1555: \n1556: ### Track B (Can start after Simulation Engine):\n1557: \n1558: - Phase Management → UI Overlay → Phase Status Display\n1559: - Canvas Rendering → Grid Interaction\n1560: \n1561: ### Track C (Can start after Simulation Engine):\n1562: \n1563: - User Interaction → Audio Sonification → Visual Polish\n1564: - Flux Management → Grid Interaction\n1565: \n1566: ### Track D (Can start after Canvas Rendering + User Interaction + Flux Management):\n1567: \n1568: - Grid Integration → Playable MVP\n1569: \n1570: ### Track E (Can start after MVP):\n1571: \n1572: - Intro Overlay → Main UI Controls → Settings Panel\n1573: - Movement Detection → Scoring System → Level Progression\n1574: \n1575: ### Track F (Can start after Level Progression):\n1576: \n1577: - Transition System → Victory Screen\n1578: \n1579: ### Track G (Can start after Scoring + Level Progression):\n1580: \n1581: - Audio Sonification → Visual Polish → Mobile Enhancements\n1582: \n1583: ### Track H (Can start after all features):\n1584: \n1585: - Expert Settings → Presets → Error Handling → Accessibility → Performance → Testing → Documentation\n1586: \n1587: ---\n1588: \n1589: ## Critical Path (Sequential Must-Haves for MVP):\n1590: \n1591: 1. **Project Setup** → Build system\n1592: 2. **Type Definitions** → All type-safe development\n1593: 3. **Shared Utilities** → Validation and state management\n1594: 4. **Simulation Engine** → Core gameplay logic\n1595: 5. **Phase Management with COUNTDOWN** → Game flow control\n1596: 6. **Canvas Rendering** → Visual feedback\n1597: 7. **User Interaction** → Input handling\n1598: 8. **Flux Management** → Resource system\n1599: 9. **Grid Integration** → Playable MVP\n1600: \n1601: ## Testing Milestones:\n1602: \n1603: - **After Sprint 1**: MVP manually playable (place cells, watch simulation, all phases work)\n1604: - **After Sprint 2**: Full game UI (intro, controls, scoring, settings)\n1605: - **After Sprint 3**: Complete game loop (intro → levels → transitions → victory)\n1606: - **After Sprint 4**: Audio and polish (all sounds, visual enhancements, mobile support)\n1607: - **After Sprint 5**: Expert settings and customization\n1608: - **After Sprint 6**: Production-ready with stability, accessibility, performance, tests, and docs\n1609: \n1610: ## Success Criteria:\n1611: \n1612: - [ ] Playable MVP after Sprint 1 (can place cells and run simulation with all phases)\n1613: - [ ] Complete UI after Sprint 2 (intro, controls, settings)\n1614: - [ ] Full game loop after Sprint 3 (intro → levels → scoring → transitions → victory)\n1615: - [ ] Audio and polish after Sprint 4 (all sounds, animations, mobile support)\n1616: - [ ] All features implemented after Sprint 5 (expert settings, presets)\n1617: - [ ] Production-ready after Sprint 6 (stability, accessibility, performance, tests, docs)\n1618: - [ ] 60fps performance with 500+ cells\n1619: - [ ] Works on mobile and desktop\n1620: - [ ] Audio works across all major browsers\n1621: - [ ] No console errors or warnings in production\n1622: - [ ] High score persistence works\n1623: - [ ] Expert settings properly configure all systems\n1624: - [ ] All critical edge cases handled gracefully\n1625: - [ ] Accessible keyboard navigation\n1626: - [ ] Comprehensive test coverage for core systems\n1627: - [ ] Clear documentation for developers and players\n1628: \n1629: ## Framework Decisions (MAKE THESE FIRST):\n\n(File has more lines. Use 'offset' parameter to read beyond line 1629)\n</content>","title":"IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md","metadata":{"preview":"- Integrated into Game.tsx to toggle settings panel\n- Follows existing patterns for timeout management and cleanup\n- All 341 tests passing\n\n**Technical Decisions:**\n\n- Uses useRef for tap tracking (avoid re-renders)\n- Implements resetTapState function inside useEffect closure for access to refs\n- Configurable threshold zone for corner detection\n- Supports both touch (touchstart) and mouse (click) events\n- Prevents default on touch events to avoid conflicts with game controls\n- Cleanup removes event listeners and clears timeout\n- Time window: 500ms between taps (standard gesture timing)\n\n**Test Coverage:**\n\n- All existing 341 tests continue to pass\n- Gesture detection verified through manual testing\n- Hook follows React best practices for event handling\n","truncated":true,"loaded":[]},"time":{"start":1771218351091,"end":1771218351099}}}}
