{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771218362317,"sessionID":"ses_39b28f7acffeLHlrypWKneG5Bj","part":{"id":"prt_c64d75fc6001BTzyMmunkxs23K","sessionID":"ses_39b28f7acffeLHlrypWKneG5Bj","messageID":"msg_c64d734bf0012IFSDhenonlSeG","type":"tool","callID":"call_7b9022ae53ab4cc78fc032a0","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md","limit":500,"offset":1629},"output":"<path>/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>1629: ## Framework Decisions (MAKE THESE FIRST):\n1630: \n1631: - **Framework**: React/Vite (recommended for performance and DX)\n1632: - **State Management**: React hooks (useState, useReducer, useRef) - minimal, no external library needed\n1633: - **Styling**: CSS modules or vanilla CSS with CSS variables for theming\n1634: - **Testing**: Vitest (fast, compatible with Vite)\n1635: - **Build Tool**: Vite (recommended for speed and simplicity)\n1636: \n1637: ## Implementation Order Recommendations:\n1638: \n1639: ### Week 1: Foundation\n1640: \n1641: 1. Project setup (Day 1)\n1642: 2. Type definitions (Day 1)\n1643: 3. Shared utilities (Day 2)\n1644: 4. Simulation engine (Day 2-3)\n1645: 5. Phase management with COUNTDOWN (Day 3-4)\n1646: 6. Canvas rendering (Day 4)\n1647: \n1648: ### Week 2: Interaction & UI\n1649: \n1650: 7. User interaction (Day 1)\n1651: 8. Flux management (Day 1-2)\n1652: 9. Grid interaction (Day 2) - MVP milestone reached\n1653: 10. Intro overlay (Day 3)\n1654: 11. Main UI controls (Day 3-4)\n1655: 12. Phase status display (Day 4)\n1656: \n1657: ### Week 3: Scoring & Progression\n1658: \n1659: 13. Movement detection (Day 1-2)\n1660: 14. Scoring system (Day 2-3)\n1661: 15. Settings panel (Day 3)\n1662: 16. Level progression (Day 4)\n1663: \n1664: ### Week 4: Transitions & Audio\n1665: \n1666: 17. Transition system (Day 1-2)\n1667: 18. Victory screen (Day 2)\n1668: 19. Audio sonification (Day 3-4)\n1669: 20. Visual polish (Day 4)\n1670: \n1671: ### Week 5: Advanced Features\n1672: \n1673: 21. Expert settings (Day 1-3)\n1674: 22. Mobile enhancements (Day 3)\n1675: 23. Presets system (Day 4)\n1676: \n1677: ### Week 6: Quality Assurance\n1678: \n1679: 24. Error handling (Day 1)\n1680: 25. Accessibility (Day 1-2)\n1681: 26. Performance optimization (Day 2)\n1682: 27. Testing (Day 3-4)\n1683: 28. Documentation (Day 4)\n1684: \n1685: ## Notes:\n1686: \n1687: - Update status (checkmark) as tasks are completed\n1688: - The plan is prioritized: CRITICAL first, then HIGH, MEDIUM, LOW\n1689: - Parallel tracks enable concurrent work where dependencies allow\n1690: - Focus on MVP first, then incrementally add polish\n1691: - src/lib/ is project's standard library for shared utilities\n1692: - Prefer consolidated implementations in src/lib/ over ad-hoc copies\n1693: - Always run lint and typecheck commands after completing features\n1694: - Test on both desktop and mobile throughout development\n1695: - Gather user feedback during development to improve UX\n1696: - Document decisions and trade-offs in comments or docs\n1697: - Keep code modular and maintainable for future enhancements\n1698: \n1699: ## Recent Progress:\n1700: \n1701: **Current Status (2026-02-16):**\n1702: \n1703: - **Sprint 1-5 Complete**: MVP, scoring, levels, transitions, audio, visual polish, mobile, and expert settings fully implemented\n1704: - **Sprint 6 In Progress**: Error Boundary completed, remaining items (accessibility, performance, testing, documentation) pending\n1705: - **All 364 tests passing** with comprehensive coverage of implemented features\n1706: - **Production-ready core game** with complete feature set\n1707: \n1708: **Recent Completion:**\n1709: \n1710: - **Sprint 6.1 Error Boundary**: Implemented global error boundary with user-friendly error UI, development-mode error details, and reload functionality. All 4 tests passing.\n1711: \n1712: ---\n1713: \n1714: **Documentation Update (2026-02-16):**\n1715: \n1716: - Updated IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md to mark Error Boundary as complete (Sprint 6.1, lines 1300-1303)\n1717: - Cleaned up Recent Progress section by removing outdated turn summaries\n1718: - Consolidated progress notes for better readability and maintainability\n1719: - Documentation now reflects current implementation state accurately\n1720: \n1721: ---\n1722: \n1723: **Turn Summary (2026-02-16):**\n1724: \n1725: - **Error Boundary (v0.0.1)**: Implemented global error boundary in Sprint 6.1 with user-friendly error UI, development-mode error details, reload functionality, and 4 tests passing\n1726: - **Reduced Motion Support (v0.0.2)**: Implemented accessibility support in Sprint 6.2 by adding prefers-reduced-motion media queries to all 10 CSS files, disabling 76 animation/transition instances for users with motion sensitivity\n1727: \n\n(End of file - total 1727 lines)\n</content>","title":"IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md","metadata":{"preview":"## Framework Decisions (MAKE THESE FIRST):\n\n- **Framework**: React/Vite (recommended for performance and DX)\n- **State Management**: React hooks (useState, useReducer, useRef) - minimal, no external library needed\n- **Styling**: CSS modules or vanilla CSS with CSS variables for theming\n- **Testing**: Vitest (fast, compatible with Vite)\n- **Build Tool**: Vite (recommended for speed and simplicity)\n\n## Implementation Order Recommendations:\n\n### Week 1: Foundation\n\n1. Project setup (Day 1)\n2. Type definitions (Day 1)\n3. Shared utilities (Day 2)\n4. Simulation engine (Day 2-3)\n5. Phase management with COUNTDOWN (Day 3-4)\n6. Canvas rendering (Day 4)\n\n### Week 2: Interaction & UI","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"time":{"start":1771218362311,"end":1771218362314}}}}
