me/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/CanvasGrid.tsx` (Line 95) - Used for cell birth/death animation timing\n- `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/ScoreDisplay.tsx` (Line 75) - Used for score number animation (200ms duration)\n- `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/FluxDisplay.tsx` (Line 42) - Used for flux value animation (300ms duration)\n- `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/GridInteraction.tsx` (Lines 63, 82, 106) - Used for cell birth/death animation timestamps\n\n### 4. Performance Metrics Logging\n**Status: LIMITED**\n- **Existing:** Basic logger utility at `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/lib/logger.ts`\n  - Provides timestamped logging with levels: debug, info, warn, error\n  - Format: `[timestamp] [LEVEL][context] message`\n  - Only logs in development mode (`import.meta.env.DEV`)\n  - **No performance-specific metrics logging**\n\n- **Animation Frame Usage:**\n  - `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/CanvasGrid.tsx` (Lines 46, 195, 202-203) - Uses `requestAnimationFrame` for rendering animations\n  - `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/ScoreDisplay.tsx` (Lines 91, 97) - Uses `requestAnimationFrame` for smooth number transitions\n  - `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/FluxDisplay.tsx` (Lines 53, 60) - Uses `requestAnimationFrame` for value animations\n  - `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/Game.tsx` (Lines 127, 237) - Uses `requestAnimationFrame` for UI state updates\n\n- **Date.now() Usage (Basic Timing):**\n  - `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/hooks/useTripleTapGesture.ts` (Line 23) - Tap gesture timing\n  - `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/hooks/useTransition.ts` (Line 144) - Transition timing\n  - `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/hooks/usePhaseTimer.ts` (Lines 37, 44) - Timer visibility change tracking\n\n---\n\n## FILE LOCATIONS FOR PERFORMANCE-RELATED CODE\n\n### Animation/Timing Files:\n1. `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/CanvasGrid.tsx` - Canvas rendering with animation frames\n2. `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/ScoreDisplay.tsx` - Score animation timing\n3. `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/FluxDisplay.tsx` - Flux animation timing\n4. `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/GridInteraction.tsx` - Cell interaction animations\n5. `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/hooks/usePhaseTimer.ts` - Phase timing with visibility tracking\n6. `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/hooks/useTransition.ts` - Transition timing\n7. `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/hooks/useTripleTapGesture.ts` - Gesture timing\n\n### Core Game Files:\n8. `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/Game.tsx` - Main game loop (uses `setInterval` at 200ms for simulation)\n9. `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/lib/simulation.ts` - Simulation logic (no performance tracking)\n10. `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/lib/logger.ts` - Logging utility (not performance-specific)\n\n### UI/Display Files:\n11. `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/GlassHUD.tsx` - HUD display (shows game stats, no performance metrics)\n\n---\n\n## PERFORMANCE METRICS THAT COULD BE ADDED\n\n### 1. FPS Monitoring\n- Real-time frame rate calculation\n- FPS history tracking\n- FPS warning thresholds (e.g., below 30 FPS)\n- Min/max FPS display\n\n### 2. Memory Monitoring\n- Heap size tracking (where available)\n- Memory usage trends\n- Memory leak detection\n- Peak memory usage logging\n\n### 3. Simulation Performance\n- Time per simulation step\n- Generation calculation duration\n- Grid size vs performance metrics\n- Pattern detection performance (movement tracking, cluster analysis)\n\n### 4. Rendering Performance\n- Canvas draw time per frame\n- Number of cells rendered\n- Animation frame timing statistics\n- Device pixel ratio impact\n\n### 5. Game-Specific Metrics\n- Active cells count impact on performance\n- Number of tracked clusters (movers, oscillators, static)\n- Interaction latency (click to render)\n- Flux placement timing\n\n---\n\n## RECOMMENDATIONS FOR PERFORMANCE TRACKING\n\n### Priority 1: Essential Metrics\n1. **Add FPS Counter**\n   - Create a new component or integrate into GlassHUD\n   - Use `requestAnimationFrame` to calculate actual FPS\n   - Display in development mode, optional in production\n\n2. **Add Simulation Step Timing**\n   - Measure duration of `stepSimulation()` function\n   - Log when steps take longer than expected threshold\n   - Track average/peak simulation times\n\n3. **Add Rendering Performance Metrics**\n   - Measure canvas draw time in `CanvasGrid.tsx`\n   - Track number of active cells vs render time\n   - Monitor animation frame consistency\n\n### Priority 2: Advanced Metrics\n4. **Memory Monitoring**\n   - Add memory tracking where `performance.memory` is available (Chrome-based browsers)\n   - Log memory trends over time\n   - Alert on memory growth patterns\n\n5. **Performance Profiling Mode**\n   - Add debug mode toggle in SettingsPanel\n   - When enabled, collect detailed metrics\n   - Export performance data for analysis\n\n6. **Batch Rendering Optimization Tracking**\n   - Monitor canvas draw calls\n   - Track cell color calculations\n   - Measure blur/shadow rendering costs\n\n### Implementation Strategy:\n\n**File: `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/lib/performance.ts`** (NEW)\n```typescript\n// Performance monitoring utility\n- FPS counter class\n- Performance timer class\n- Memory monitor class\n- Metrics collector\n```\n\n**File: `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/hooks/usePerformanceMonitor.ts`** (NEW)\n```typescript\n// React hook for performance monitoring\n- FPS tracking hook\n- Component render time tracking\n- Simulation timing hook\n```\n\n**Modify: `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/GlassHUD.tsx`**\n- Add optional performance stats display\n- Show FPS in development mode\n- Display current simulation step time\n\n**Modify: `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/lib/logger.ts`**\n- Add performance-specific log methods\n- Log timing metrics with context\n- Add performance data export\n\n### Best Practices for Implementation:\n1. **Development vs Production**: Only show detailed metrics in development mode\n2. **Performance Overhead**: Ensure monitoring doesn't significantly impact performance\n3. **Thresholds**: Set configurable warning thresholds for FPS, render time, etc.\n4. **History**: Keep configurable history of metrics for trend analysis\n5. **Export**: Provide ability to export performance data for analysis\n6. **Toggleable**: Make performance monitoring optional and toggleable via settings\n\n### Specific Integration Points:\n- **Game.tsx**: Add timing around `handleSimulationStep()` \n- **CanvasGrid.tsx**: Add render timing measurements\n- **simulation.ts**: Add timing around `applyRules()` and `findConnectedComponents()`\n- **movement.ts**: Add timing for cluster tracking calculations\n- **GlassHUD.tsx**: Add performance stats display section\n\nThis codebase currently has minimal performance monitoring, focusing only on animation timing rather than overall performance metrics. Implementing the recommendations above would provide comprehensive visibility into the game's performance characteristics.\n</task_result>","title":"Find performance monitoring code","metadata":{"sessionId":"ses_39b2640cfffeZ9d0ymiCKDv4JC","model":{"modelID":"glm-4.7","providerID":"zai-coding-plan"},"truncated":false},"time":{"start":1771218517806,"end":1771218593049}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771218599523,"sessionID":"ses_39b28f7acffeLHlrypWKneG5Bj","part":{"id":"prt_c64d9bf02001U1lUZ0MuQzJdUx","sessionID":"ses_39b28f7acffeLHlrypWKneG5Bj","messageID":"msg_c64d95932001EIAqaWUJl7M55r","type":"tool","callID":"call_90313b814ad3463f968f3c85","tool":"task","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"description":"Find browser compatibility code","prompt":"Search the codebase in /home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src for browser compatibility handling:\n1. Web Audio API feature detection\n2. Canvas API feature detection\n3. Any browser-specific fallbacks\n4. Feature checks before using APIs\n\nLook for:\n- `window.AudioContext` or `webkitAudioContext` usage\n- `document.createElement('canvas')`\n- Any checks like `if (!window.Feature)` \n- Browser-specific prefixes\n- Polyfills or fallback implementations\n\nReturn a summary of:\n- What browser compatibility checks exist\n- What features are used without checks\n- Recommended checks that should be added\n- File locations for any compatibility code","subagent_type":"explore"},"output":"task_id: ses_39b2640f9ffebs9p6WuDLBoTDQ (for resuming to continue this task if needed)\n\n<task_result>\nBased on my thorough search of the `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src` directory, here's a comprehensive summary of browser compatibility handling:\n\n## Browser Compatibility Checks That Exist\n\n### 1. Web Audio API Feature Detection ✓\n**File:** `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/lib/audio.ts`\n\nThe code has proper feature detection for Web Audio API:\n```typescript\nprivate ensureAudioContext(): void {\n  if (!this.audioContext) {\n    try {\n      const AudioContextClass =\n        window.AudioContext ||\n        (window as typeof window & { webkitAudioContext?: typeof AudioContext })\n          .webkitAudioContext\n      this.audioContext = new AudioContextClass()\n    } catch (error) {\n      console.error('Error creating AudioContext:', error)\n    }\n  } else if (this.audioContext.state === 'suspended') {\n    this.audioContext.resume().catch((error) => {\n      console.error('Error resuming AudioContext:', error)\n    })\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Strengths:**\n- Falls back to `webkitAudioContext` for Safari/older browsers\n- Wrapped in try-catch to handle failures gracefully\n- Handles suspended AudioContext state\n- All audio operations check if audioContext exists before using it\n- Graceful degradation - audio features simply don't play if unsupported\n\n### 2. localStorage Error Handling ✓\n**Files:** \n- `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/lib/state.ts`\n- `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/lib/level.ts`\n\nBoth files have proper try-catch blocks around localStorage operations:\n```typescript\nexport function saveToLocalStorage<T>(key: string, value: T): boolean {\n  try {\n    const fullKey = `${STORAGE_KEY_PREFIX}${key}`\n    const serialized = JSON.stringify(value)\n    localStorage.setItem(fullKey, serialized)\n    return true\n  } catch (error) {\n    console.error('Failed to save to localStorage:', error)\n    return false\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Strengths:**\n- All localStorage operations wrapped in try-catch\n- Returns boolean to indicate success/failure\n- Falls back to default values on load failures\n- Handles cases where localStorage might be disabled (e.g., private browsing)\n\n---\n\n## Features Used Without Checks ⚠️\n\n### 1. Canvas 2D API - `roundRect()` Method\n**File:** `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/CanvasGrid.tsx` (lines 133, 164, 181)\n\nThe code uses `ctx.roundRect()` which has limited browser support:\n```typescript\nctx.roundRect(x + 1, y + 1, actualCellSize - 2, actualCellSize - 2, radius)\n```\n\n**Browser Support:** \n- Chrome 99+\n- Firefox 112+\n- Safari 16+\n- **NOT supported in older browsers**\n\n**Recommended:** Add feature detection or polyfill:\n```typescript\nif (!ctx.roundRect) {\n  // Fallback: use rect() instead\n  ctx.rect(x + 1, y + 1, actualCellSize - 2, actualCellSize - 2)\n} else {\n  ctx.roundRect(x + 1, y + 1, actualCellSize - 2, actualCellSize - 2, radius)\n}\n```\n\n### 2. Canvas.getContext('2d')\n**File:** `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/CanvasGrid.tsx` (line 54)\n\nThe code checks if context exists but doesn't validate canvas support:\n```typescript\nconst ctx = canvas.getContext('2d')\nif (!ctx) return\n```\n\n**Status:** ✓ Good - properly checks for null context\n\n### 3. requestAnimationFrame / cancelAnimationFrame\n**Files:**\n- `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/CanvasGrid.tsx` (lines 195, 203)\n- `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/ScoreDisplay.tsx` (lines 91, 97)\n- `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/FluxDisplay.tsx` (lines 38, 53, 60, 64)\n- `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/Game.tsx` (lines 127, 237)\n\n**Status:** ⚠️ Used without checks, but good browser support (IE10+)\n\n**Recommended:** Add vendor prefix fallbacks for very old browsers:\n```typescript\nconst requestAnimationFrame = \n  window.requestAnimationFrame || \n  window.webkitRequestAnimationFrame ||\n  (callback => setTimeout(callback, 16))\n```\n\n### 4. devicePixelRatio\n**File:** `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/CanvasGrid.tsx` (line 57)\n\n```typescript\nconst dpr = window.devicePixelRatio || 1\n```\n\n**Status:** ✓ Good - has fallback to 1\n\n### 5. performance.now()\n**Files:**\n- `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/CanvasGrid.tsx` (line 95)\n- `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/ScoreDisplay.tsx` (line 75)\n- `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/FluxDisplay.tsx` (line 42)\n- `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/GridInteraction.tsx` (lines 63, 82, 106)\n\n**Status:** ⚠️ Used without checks, but good browser support (IE10+)\n\n**Recommended:** Add fallback for very old browsers:\n```typescript\nconst now = window.performance ? window.performance.now() : Date.now()\n```\n\n### 6. Touch Events\n**Files:**\n- `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/hooks/useTripleTapGesture.ts` (line 54)\n- `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/lib/interaction.ts` (line 23)\n\n**Status:** ⚠️ Used without checks, but good browser support (mobile browsers)\n\n**Recommended:** Add feature detection before attaching touch listeners:\n```typescript\nif ('ontouchstart' in window) {\n  window.addEventListener('touchstart', handleTouchStart, { passive: false })\n}\n```\n\n### 7. CSS Custom Properties (CSS Variables)\n**File:** `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/CanvasGrid.tsx` (line 188)\n\n```typescript\ndocument.documentElement.style.setProperty('--life-intensity', intensity.toString())\n```\n\n**Status:** ⚠️ Used without checks, but good browser support (IE11+ not supported)\n\n### 8. React.createRoot\n**File:** `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/main.tsx` (line 6)\n\n```typescript\ncreateRoot(document.getElementById('root')!).render(\n```\n\n**Status:** ⚠️ React 19's createRoot API - requires modern browsers (no IE support)\n\n---\n\n## Recommended Checks That Should Be Added\n\n### High Priority\n\n1. **Canvas roundRect polyfill** (`/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/CanvasGrid.tsx`):\n   - Add feature detection for `ctx.roundRect`\n   - Provide fallback to `ctx.rect` or `ctx.arcTo`\n\n2. **Touch event detection** (`/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/hooks/useTripleTapGesture.ts`):\n   - Only attach touch listeners if touch is supported\n   - Prevents errors on non-touch devices\n\n3. **requestAnimationFrame polyfill** (in utility file or directly):\n   - Add vendor prefix fallbacks for Safari 6 and IE9\n\n### Medium Priority\n\n4. **performance.now() fallback**:\n   - Add fallback to `Date.now()` for very old browsers\n\n5. **Canvas support detection** (in CanvasGrid component initialization):\n   - Check if `<canvas>` element is supported before rendering\n\n6. **CSS Variables fallback**:\n   - Detect CSS custom property support\n   - Provide fallback styling for older browsers\n\n### Low Priority\n\n7. **Local storage availability check** (in state.ts initialization):\n   - Add a check on app startup to detect if localStorage is available\n   - Currently handled by try-catch, but could be more proactive\n\n---\n\n## File Locations Summary\n\n### Files WITH Good Compatibility Code:\n- `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/lib/audio.ts` - Web Audio API with webkitAudioContext fallback\n- `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/lib/state.ts` - localStorage with try-catch\n- `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/lib/level.ts` - localStorage with try-catch\n\n### Files REQUIRING Compatibility Improvements:\n- `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/CanvasGrid.tsx` - roundRect() needs polyfill\n- `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/hooks/useTripleTapGesture.ts` - Touch events need detection\n- `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/ScoreDisplay.tsx` - requestAnimationFrame and performance.now() \n- `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/FluxDisplay.tsx` - requestAnimationFrame and performance.now()\n- `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/Game.tsx` - requestAnimationFrame\n- `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/main.tsx` - createRoot (React 19)\n\n---\n\n## CSS Browser Prefixes\nThe codebase uses vendor prefixes in CSS files for browser compatibility:\n- `-webkit-font-smoothing`\n- `-moz-osx-font-smoothing`\n- `-webkit-appearance` (for sliders)\n- `-webkit-slider-thumb`, `-moz-range-thumb` (for slider styling)\n\nThese are in: `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/styles/` files\n\n---\n\n## Overall Assessment\n\n**Strengths:**\n- Excellent Web Audio API compatibility handling with vendor prefixes\n- Good localStorage error handling\n- Appropriate use of try-catch blocks around potentially failing operations\n- Audio features gracefully degrade if unsupported\n\n**Weaknesses:**\n- `ctx.roundRect()` will break in older browsers (needs polyfill)\n- Touch event listeners not feature-detected\n- Modern APIs (requestAnimationFrame, performance.now) used without legacy fallbacks\n- React 19 creates de facto requirement for modern browsers\n- No polyfills included in the build process\n\n**Build Configuration:**\n- TypeScript target: ES2020 (from tsconfig.json)\n- No browser compatibility targets configured in vite.config.ts\n- No polyfill configuration present\n\nThe codebase would work well in modern browsers (Chrome 99+, Firefox 112+, Safari 16+, Edge 99+), but would have issues in older browsers, particularly Internet Explorer or Safari versions prior to 16.\n</task_result>","title":"Find browser compatibility code","metadata":{"sessionId":"ses_39b2640f9ffebs9p6WuDLBoTDQ","model":{"modelID":"glm-4.7","providerID":"zai-coding-plan"},"truncated":false},"time":{"start":1771218517765,"end":1771218599520}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771218608244,"sessionID":"ses_39b28f7acffeLHlrypWKneG5Bj","part":{"id":"prt_c64d9a775001sut9bcY8joY8bm","sessionID":"ses_39b28f7acffeLHlrypWKneG5Bj","messageID":"msg_c64d95932001EIAqaWUJl7M55r","type":"tool","callID":"call_138fd6c1fd0b4ece897d0813","tool":"task","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"description":"Find edge case handling gaps","prompt":"Search the codebase in /home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src for any edge case handling related to:\n1. Empty grid states\n2. Zero flux scenarios\n3. Invalid level numbers\n4. Corrupted localStorage\n\nLook for any error handling, validation, or fallback code related to these scenarios. Check:\n- All .ts and .tsx files in src/\n- Look for try/catch blocks\n- Look for validation functions\n- Look for error boundary usage\n\nReturn a summary of:\n- What edge case handling is currently implemented\n- What edge cases are NOT handled but should be\n- File locations for any relevant code found","subagent_type":"explore"},"output":"task_id: ses_39b265887ffeWZouyxgCDdXQv4 (for resuming to continue this task if needed)\n\n<task_result>\nBased on my comprehensive search of the codebase, here's a detailed summary of edge case handling:\n\n---\n\n## Edge Case Handling Summary\n\n### 1. Empty Grid States\n\n**Currently Implemented:**\n\n**File: `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/lib/simulation.ts`**\n- `isGridEmpty()` (line 135): Checks if countAliveCells returns 0\n- `countAliveCells()` (line 113): Returns 0 for empty grids\n- `createGrid()` (line 26): Initializes all cells to 0\n\n**File: `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/lib/phase.ts`**\n- `getBlockers()` (line 33-38): Prevents starting without cells with error message \"Need at least 1 cell to start\"\n\n**File: `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/Game.tsx`**\n- `hasCells()` callback (line 179): Used to check grid state before starting\n- `handleStart()` (line 298): Validates `hasCells()` before allowing start\n\n**Test Coverage:** `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/lib/simulation.test.ts` (lines 279-290)\n\n**NOT Handled:**\n- No explicit UI feedback when grid becomes empty during RUNNING phase\n- No warning if all cells die out naturally during simulation\n- No special handling for \"dead end\" patterns that leave no alive cells\n\n---\n\n### 2. Zero Flux Scenarios\n\n**Currently Implemented:**\n\n**File: `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/lib/flux.ts`**\n- `canPlaceCell()` (line 12): Returns false if flux < 1\n- `placeCell()` (line 20): Returns unchanged flux if cannot place\n- `getFluxColor()` (line 51-56): Returns 'red' when flux === 0\n- Flux is clamped to minimum 5 in level generation\n\n**File: `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/GridInteraction.tsx`**\n- Lines 69-90: Plays error sound and shows visual feedback when trying to place with zero flux\n- Lines 176-178: Cursor changes to 'not-allowed' when flux is 0\n- `isPlaceable()` (line 183): Returns false when flux is 0\n\n**File: `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/lib/level.ts`**\n- Lines 21, 26, 31: `Math.max(5, ...)` ensures flux never goes below 5\n\n**NOT Handled:**\n- No recovery mechanism if user runs out of flux during PLANNING phase\n- No warning that level may be impossible to complete with low flux\n- No \"flux refill\" or bonus mechanism\n\n---\n\n### 3. Invalid Level Numbers\n\n**Currently Implemented:**\n\n**File: `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/lib/level.ts`**\n- `getCurrentLevelConfig()` (lines 83-88): Returns `null` for invalid level numbers (< 1 or > length)\n- Level arrays are generated starting from index 0 with `levelNumber: i` (line 52)\n- Tests verify null return for invalid level (level.test.ts line 195)\n\n**File: `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/Game.tsx`**\n- Line 123: `const currentLevelConfig = getCurrentLevelConfig(levelProgression)`\n- Line 158: Null coalescing `??` used for `initialFlux` fallback\n- Line 419: Null coalescing `??` used for `initialFlux` in victory screen\n\n**NOT Handled:**\n- No validation of `levelNumber` parameter type (could be negative, float, or NaN)\n- No explicit error handling when `currentLevelConfig` is null\n- No user-friendly message if accessing non-existent level\n- `generateLevelConfig()` doesn't validate input parameters (line 7)\n\n---\n\n### 4. Corrupted localStorage\n\n**Currently Implemented:**\n\n**File: `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/lib/state.ts`**\n- **saveToLocalStorage()** (lines 79-89): try/catch wraps setItem, returns false on error, logs error\n- **loadFromLocalStorage()** (lines 91-102): try/catch wraps getItem/JSON.parse, returns defaultValue on error, handles parse errors\n- **removeFromLocalStorage()** (lines 104-113): try/catch wraps removeItem, returns false on error\n\n**File: `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/lib/level.ts`**\n- **loadHighScores()** (lines 130-140): try/catch for JSON.parse, returns empty object on error, logs warning\n- **saveHighScores()** (lines 142-148): try/catch for setItem, logs warning on error\n\n**File: `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/lib/settings.ts`**\n- Uses `saveToLocalStorage` and `loadFromLocalStorage` with default values (lines 50-55)\n\n**Test Coverage:** `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/lib/state.test.ts` (lines 157-247)\n\n**NOT Handled:**\n- No detection of localStorage being disabled (quota exceeded, privacy mode)\n- No migration strategy for data format changes\n- No way to reset corrupted data without manual intervention\n- Quota exceeded errors treated same as other errors (no specific handling)\n- No validation that loaded data matches expected schema\n\n---\n\n### 5. Additional Edge Case Handling Found\n\n**Error Boundary:**\n- File: `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/ErrorBoundary.tsx`\n- Catches React component errors, displays user-friendly message\n- Shows error details in development mode\n- Provides reload button to recover\n\n**Input Validation:**\n- File: `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/lib/validation.ts`\n- Validates grid dimensions (max 1000x1000, must be positive)\n- Validates rule sets and coordinate bounds\n- Type guards for number validation\n\n**Settings Validation:**\n- File: `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/lib/settings.ts` (lines 28-127)\n- `validateExpertSettings()` validates all setting parameters with ranges\n- File: `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/SettingsPanel.tsx` (lines 11-17)\n- `validateExpertSettingsDetailed()` provides detailed error messages for import\n\n**Audio Error Handling:**\n- File: `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/lib/audio.ts`\n- All audio operations wrapped in try/catch (lines 49-256)\n- Gracefully handles AudioContext creation/resume failures\n- Continues silently if audio fails\n\n**Coordinate Validation:**\n- File: `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/lib/interaction.ts`\n- `isWithinBounds()` (lines 40-47): Checks row/col are within grid bounds\n- Used throughout GridInteraction component\n\n---\n\n### Recommendations for Missing Edge Cases\n\n1. **Empty Grid during RUNNING phase**: Add \"Game Over\" state if all cells die\n2. **Zero Flux recovery**: Add mechanism to restart level or get flux refill\n3. **Invalid level numbers**: Add explicit validation and user-friendly error messages\n4. **localStorage quota exceeded**: Detect and provide \"Reset Data\" option\n5. **Schema validation**: Validate loaded localStorage data structure before use\n6. **NaN/Infinity handling**: Add guards in scoring and flux calculations\n7. **Concurrent mutations**: Guard against rapid successive state updates causing race conditions\n</task_result>","title":"Find edge case handling gaps","metadata":{"sessionId":"ses_39b265887ffeWZouyxgCDdXQv4","model":{"modelID":"glm-4.7","providerID":"zai-coding-plan"},"truncated":false},"time":{"start":1771218511735,"end":1771218608242}}}}
